# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEFECTS FOUND BY RUNNING THEM
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

defect def:compress-savings-compares-unlike-quantities
  status OPEN
  verification REPRODUCED
  symptom on schemas/ it reports raw 7,635 vs compressed 12,129 for savings_pct -58.9%, claiming compression enlarged the data; on packs/ it reports raw_bytes 0 against compressed 2,963,629 for 0.0% savings
  cause raw is summed FILE bytes while compressed is a compressed TAR, so tar block padding dominates small corpora
  not_broken the compression itself is correct -- 2,963,629 matches an independent tar|zstd-19 reference exactly
  independent_measure .yaff/.json subsets compress 3.8x (packs) and 7.7x (architecture) at zstd-19

defect def:query-stats-selects-a-column-scan-never-writes
  status OPEN
  verification REPRODUCED
  symptom bonfyre-query stats fails with 'Binder Error: Referenced column "type" not found in FROM clause! Candidate bindings: "filename"'
  scope scan works and imported 594 artifacts; the sql subcommand works on the same store; only the canned stats query is broken

defect def:capability-match-is-lexical-not-semantic
  status OPEN
  verification REPRODUCED
  symptom advertised as 'semantic match' using a 'native semantic registry', but scores are clean fractions of query-term overlap (0.167, 0.333) and a query whose words are absent returns an unscored fallback
  works 'compress an artifact to save space' finds bonfyre-fpq and bonfyre-pack; 'route inference to the cheapest model' finds bonfyre-model and bonfyre-sli
  fails 'classify business type from a company name' returns brief, offer and threshold-tune while tag-artifact/bonfyre-tag -- the correct answer, present in the registry -- never surfaces
  available_fix bonfyre-embed onnx plus bonfyre-vec are used elsewhere in this session and are not behind this verb

defect def:bonfyre-model-fails-on-large-transfers
  status OPEN
  verification REPRODUCED
  symptom pull of a 1,840 MB gguf reached 1,162 MB then reported 'source failed, trying next' and deleted the partial
  source_is_fine HEAD returns 200 and a ranged GET returns 1,046 bytes with a 302 follow, so the URL serves correctly
  contrast an 80 MB gguf pulled successfully earlier in the session
  also the registered source for llama-3-8b-instruct is the GATED meta-llama repo, which fails for any unauthenticated pull
  workaround file:// is an accepted source scheme, so a sideloaded file can be registered
  consequence local generation remains unproven for want of a transfer, not a capability

defect def:bonfyre-tag-claims-pure-c
  status OPEN
  verification REPRODUCED
  symptom banner reads 'instant topic/intent tagging (fastText, pure C)' but the binary shells to a generated Python script importing fasttext; training failed with ModuleNotFoundError until fasttext-wheel was installed
  note the capability is real and fast; the claim and the missing startup dependency check are the defect

